WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.634
-Our first guest is
an Emmy-winning actor

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:05.300
who stars
in "The Righteous Gemstones,"

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.300
which airs Sundays
at 10:00 pm on HBO.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.567
[ Drumroll ]
Ladies and gentlemen,
please welcome John Goodman!

00:00:11.567 --> 00:00:13.200
[ Cheering and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.234
-Oh!
[ Laughs ]

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:17.601
Yes!

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:19.601
Finally. I love this!

00:00:19.601 --> 00:00:21.267
-This is fanta--
-Thank you, Jimmy.

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:22.934
-I love this.
This is fantastic.

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:24.634
John Goodman,
thank you for being here

00:00:24.634 --> 00:00:26.000
and thanks for being
on the show.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.133
It is nice to see you.

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:29.434
That is a beautiful --

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:30.701
Is that your living room?

00:00:30.701 --> 00:00:32.234
Is that where you are?

00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:34.601
-That's one of my living rooms,
Jimmy,

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.300
[ Laughter ]
out here in California.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.701
-It's gorgeous.

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:41.400
-We propose it as a dining room
and Amazon catchall.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:42.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.734 --> 00:00:44.067
-What's been going on?

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:46.300
What's going on
in the Goodman household?

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.567
-Well, we got a wedding
coming up.

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:50.701
My daughter's getting married
in...

00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:52.434
-No way! Wow!
-...March.

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:53.734
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]
So there's a lot

00:00:53.734 --> 00:00:55.167
of planning involved.

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:56.334
A lot of planning.

00:00:56.334 --> 00:00:57.901
-Congrats, congrats.

00:00:57.901 --> 00:00:59.234
-My idea of planning
a wedding is

00:00:59.234 --> 00:01:02.167
finding a huge,
empty garbage barrel,

00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:04.234
dumping about 10 cases of beer
in there,

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:05.467
and throwing some ice on top.

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:07.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:10.234
But my wife wants napkins
and stuff like that, so...

00:01:10.234 --> 00:01:13.367
-Ah, jeez.
-...I'm letting her do it.

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:14.434
-Are you going to make a speech

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:17.000
or do that father of the bride
stuff?

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.834
-I'm sure I'll have to.
-Yeah.

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:19.934
[ Laughter ]
-I'll find something.

00:01:19.934 --> 00:01:20.767
I'll crib something.

00:01:20.767 --> 00:01:22.300
[ Laughter ]
-[ Clap ]

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:25.634
Yeah. We're halfway
through January, John.

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:28.000
Did you make a New Year's
resolution at all?

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:31.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.501 --> 00:01:33.701
-I kind of gave them up, by now,

00:01:33.701 --> 00:01:35.868
but, over the course
of the last two years,

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:37.801
I haven't been exercising

00:01:37.801 --> 00:01:40.067
and I can't use COVID
for an excuse anymore,

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:43.300
so my wife, for Christmas,
bought me a rowing machine.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.634
-Yes!
-Yeah, it looks swell.

00:01:45.634 --> 00:01:47.200
It's got a TV on it,
and everything.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:53.200
So I can work on that
and watch TV at the same time.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.067
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:54.834
Have you done it?

00:01:54.834 --> 00:01:57.267
Have you tried it out yet?

00:01:57.267 --> 00:01:58.868
-I got it out of the box.

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:00.501
[ Laughter ]
-[ Claps ]

00:02:00.501 --> 00:02:02.133
-But, yeah, no, I did.

00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:03.067
I did it this morning.

00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:05.267
It was a guy teaching you how

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:07.934
to work a rowing machine
with a TV on it.

00:02:07.934 --> 00:02:10.501
[ Laughter ]
And that was about 13 minutes

00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:11.968
of talking,
two minutes of exercise,

00:02:11.968 --> 00:02:12.834
so I'm ready.

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:14.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.534
-John, I've said this before.

00:02:16.534 --> 00:02:19.234
You're one of my favorite actors
and I say this --

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:22.200
that, if you see John Goodman's
name on a poster,

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.467
that means you're
in for a treat,

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:26.467
a great movie, a great project.

00:02:26.467 --> 00:02:28.567
Anything I see, I go,
"John Goodman's in it?

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:31.334
I love it."

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:33.901
And it's always
a fantastic performance.

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:35.434
But I was going to ask you,
John Goodman,

00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:37.868
do you have a favorite
John Goodman performance?

00:02:37.868 --> 00:02:41.634
[ Laughter ]
-Usually, the movies that I have
the most fun on

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:44.734
are the ones that stuff
at the box office.

00:02:44.734 --> 00:02:46.133
So.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:46.133 --> 00:02:50.300
-I like, I guess,
"Big Lebowski."

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:51.567
Everybody likes it.

00:02:51.567 --> 00:02:53.033
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:53.968
Had a lot of fun.

00:02:55.901 --> 00:02:58.834
"The Big Lebowski,"
when it first came out,

00:02:58.834 --> 00:03:01.434
it was not really --
it was like mixed reviews.

00:03:01.434 --> 00:03:04.167
It wasn't that big of a hit,
was it?

00:03:04.167 --> 00:03:06.734
-I guess. I really don't
remember when it came out,

00:03:06.734 --> 00:03:09.167
but I usually don't read reviews

00:03:09.167 --> 00:03:11.100
because they hurt my feelings
real bad.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.634
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, of course. Smart, smart.

00:03:12.634 --> 00:03:14.167
-I didn't know how
it was received

00:03:14.167 --> 00:03:17.334
and I didn't pay
any attention to,

00:03:17.334 --> 00:03:19.334
You know, the entertainment
journalism, so.

00:03:19.334 --> 00:03:22.267
I knew we did something good.

00:03:22.267 --> 00:03:25.434
It just felt great and I knew
we had a terrific script,

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:27.367
so I wasn't too worried
about it.

00:03:27.367 --> 00:03:28.834
So it lives on.

00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:31.033
-Yeah. When did you realize
it was like --

00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:33.334
Because now it's like people,

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:35.434
they dress up as you and they,

00:03:35.434 --> 00:03:38.367
I mean, people reenact.

00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:40.267
There's festivals now.

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:44.033
-Yeah, I realized it was popular
when I had guys dressed like me

00:03:44.033 --> 00:03:46.601
showing up at my house
with crap for me to sign.

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:49.267
[ Laughter ]
-[ Clap ]

00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:52.200
You know, we have Cecily Strong
on the show after you.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.601
[ Laughter ]
I know, I know. We love her.

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:57.100
And I read this somewhere
and I'm curious about this

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:59.234
because I've known you
for a long time.

00:03:59.234 --> 00:04:03.334
Did you once audition
for "Saturday Night Live"?

00:04:03.334 --> 00:04:04.701
[ Laughter ]
John Goodman!

00:04:04.701 --> 00:04:07.534
John Goodman, you did?!

00:04:07.534 --> 00:04:09.267
-In 1980.

00:04:09.267 --> 00:04:12.067
-Wow!
-Yeah.

00:04:12.067 --> 00:04:15.801
Not that I had any material
to show or anything good to do.

00:04:15.801 --> 00:04:17.767
I just knew they'd hire me.

00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:19.434
[ Laughter ]
Just for my pers--

00:04:19.434 --> 00:04:20.767
because I'm a nice guy.

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:23.901
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Wow!

00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:25.801
It's the worst thing
I've ever done

00:04:25.801 --> 00:04:27.334
in front of people in my life.

00:04:27.334 --> 00:04:28.501
I wrote something

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:31.667
about 15 minutes
before I went over there and,

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:34.601
oh, God, it was awful.
-You still think about it.

00:04:34.601 --> 00:04:35.801
Isn't that weird?
You still think

00:04:35.801 --> 00:04:37.367
about those awful things, like,
"Why did I?

00:04:37.367 --> 00:04:39.133
It was so embarrassing," yeah.

00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:40.934
But you didn't get cast, but,

00:04:40.934 --> 00:04:43.567
you went on to host 13 times,
buddy.

00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:45.267
[ Cheering and applause ]
Come on, one of the best hosts

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:47.467
-Yeah.
-in the history of the show.

00:04:50.334 --> 00:04:52.901
-That used to be the favorite
thing I'd do every year,

00:04:52.901 --> 00:04:54.767
would be "Saturday Night Live."

00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:56.334
They always made me feel at home

00:04:56.334 --> 00:04:59.534
and you're with a bunch
of smart and funny people

00:04:59.534 --> 00:05:01.501
and it just feels great.

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.734
-Yeah. I've done a bunch of fun
things, great things.

00:05:03.734 --> 00:05:05.534
That's where I first met you.

00:05:05.534 --> 00:05:07.234
Do you remember we did one,
once,

00:05:07.234 --> 00:05:10.534
it was you were hosting
and Tom Petty was musical guest?

00:05:10.534 --> 00:05:12.901
And I think T. Sean Shannon
wrote it,

00:05:12.901 --> 00:05:14.234
or maybe Smigel.
I'm trying to think.

00:05:14.234 --> 00:05:16.067
But the monologue, you came out

00:05:16.067 --> 00:05:18.334
and then I asked those questions
from the audience,

00:05:18.334 --> 00:05:19.501
you know that bit?

00:05:19.501 --> 00:05:21.133
Where you go,
"Anyone have any questions?"

00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:24.834
-[ Laughing ]
-You know, "Before we start
the show --

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:26.667
[ Laughter ]
Before we start the show,

00:05:26.667 --> 00:05:28.667
does anyone have any questions?

00:05:28.667 --> 00:05:29.868
And someone stood up.

00:05:29.868 --> 00:05:31.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:33.167
But someone stood up
and they go,

00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:36.033
"I just want to ask you,
is tonight's show a repeat?"

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:38.400
[ Laughter ]
And you're like, "No,

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:39.868
no, this is a new show.

00:05:39.868 --> 00:05:41.467
This is 'Saturday Night Live'
and we're live right now,

00:05:41.467 --> 00:05:43.100
so this is not a repeat."

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:45.167
And they go, "I think I've seen
this show before.

00:05:45.167 --> 00:05:46.234
-"I've seen it."
-It's you and Tom Petty."

00:05:46.234 --> 00:05:48.100
[ Laughter ]
Yeah. And then, I sit up.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:49.968
I go, "Yeah, actually,
I've seen this show.

00:05:49.968 --> 00:05:51.467
It's very good.
It's a funny one."

00:05:51.467 --> 00:05:52.968
And you're like, "No."

00:05:52.968 --> 00:05:54.267
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.267 --> 00:05:56.501
-That was Adam McKay.

00:05:56.501 --> 00:05:57.934
-What was that,
Adam McKay wrote that?

00:05:57.934 --> 00:06:00.767
-Yeah, yeah.
-Wow! McKay, I love that.

00:06:00.767 --> 00:06:02.367
Oh, my gosh.
And look at him now.

00:06:02.367 --> 00:06:04.133
He's crushing it, huh?
With the movies.

00:06:04.133 --> 00:06:05.667
-Absolutely, man.
-He's brilliant.

00:06:05.667 --> 00:06:09.000
-He used to write
some great bits to bomb in.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:13.267
He and Will Ferrell would get
together and write something

00:06:13.267 --> 00:06:15.601
and, if they sniffed
that it was bombing,

00:06:15.601 --> 00:06:18.067
Will would just push
the throttle forward

00:06:18.067 --> 00:06:19.567
and go for it.
-Yes, exactly.

00:06:19.567 --> 00:06:21.400
-"We're going to kill everybody
in here

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:22.601
and take them with us."
-Yeah.

00:06:22.601 --> 00:06:23.534
[ Laughter ]
[ Claps ]

00:06:23.534 --> 00:06:24.501
Do you remember?

00:06:24.501 --> 00:06:25.634
I remember Will doing a bit

00:06:25.634 --> 00:06:26.968
that was not working

00:06:26.968 --> 00:06:29.467
and the cast who were not even
in the sketch

00:06:29.467 --> 00:06:31.934
would just go out to the floor
to watch him bomb.

00:06:31.934 --> 00:06:33.367
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.367 --> 00:06:34.868
Because it was so entertaining.

00:06:34.868 --> 00:06:36.033
It was so funny to watch.

00:06:36.033 --> 00:06:38.667
You were like, "Oh, my gosh.
This is tanking.

00:06:38.667 --> 00:06:41.067
No one is laughing.
It is terrible."

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:43.467
And he was like --
It was just so fun to watch

00:06:43.467 --> 00:06:45.567
and he would do it.
He would take his extra time

00:06:45.567 --> 00:06:48.033
and really milk it.
-The kid's an artist.

00:06:48.033 --> 00:06:50.267
[ Laughter ]
-He is an artist.

00:06:50.267 --> 00:06:51.667
John, when we come back,
I want to talk to you

00:06:51.667 --> 00:06:54.133
about "The Conners"
and "The Righteous Gemstones."

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:56.133
More with John Goodman
after the break.

